  "worked_solution": "The Wronskian $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})$ of two vector-valued functions \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis defined as\n\n$$\nW({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=det({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) & {x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t) & {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Wronskian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({x}_{1},{x}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2{e}^{3t}\\cdot 5{e}^{-2t}-0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =10{e}^{3t-2t} \\\\  & =10{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
